I have successfully designed and built the PhishGuard Forensics Hub, an interactive educational application designed for beginners to learn, simulate, and program a 7-step phishing detection flowchart and its accompanying continuous feedback loop.
🎨 Visual & Interactive Lab Architecture
Interactive Detection Flowchart (/src/components/FlowchartVisualizer.tsx)
Renders a responsive, visually striking 7-phase sequence spanning Email Reception, Identity & Header Scanning, Content & URL Risk Analysis, User Warnings, Blocking & Quarantine, Incident Reporting, and the Continuous Feedback Loop.
Includes real-time connector highlights, glowing active node states, and a visual curved dashed loopback path representing threat intel feedback to early filtering layers.
Highlights an Interactive Forensic Inspector drawer: Users can click any stage on the flowchart to inspect its Beginner Analogy and Under-the-Hood RFC technical specifications.
Perimeter Threat Simulator (/src/components/EmailSimulator.tsx)
Models a full-featured desktop email client. Beginners can select different email templates (such as Netflix Billing Spoofs, Google Security Warnings, HR Survey Phishes, or Legitimate Banking Invoices).
Features a Forensic Header Toggle showing raw SMTP delivery chains and SPF / DKIM DNS authentication compliance chips.
Features a Self-Study Clue Drawer where beginners can check their pattern-spotting accuracy against a curated list of phishing indicators.
Triggers a Redirection Block Page Interstitial: If a user clicks any malicious link in the sandbox, a safe mock Security Gateway blocks the request and guides them to further learning resources.
Active Learning Feedback Loop Engine (/src/App.tsx)
Runs a real-time sequential timer animating the email through each filter.
Feedback Loop Demonstration: When a user clicks 📢 Report Phishing to Firewall, the sender's lookalike domain is dynamically logged into a visible Local Blacklist Database (DNSBL).
If that template or a matching domain is simulated again, the engine executes a Short-Circuit Fast Block: Step 2 (Header Scanning) instantly flags the blacklist match and skips deep content parsing, terminating SMTP transmission and quarantining the mail immediately.
Knowledge Validation Quiz (/src/components/InteractiveQuiz.tsx)
Tests users on core email security protocols (SPF, DKIM, Lookalikes, and Quarantines) and rewards them with a forensics achievement rank badge upon completion.
Student Code Blueprints (/src/components/CodeBlueprint.tsx)
Provides fully executable, highly documented starter code in both Python and TypeScript modeling this exact flowchart logic. Ideal for copy-pasting directly into local high school or college projects!
Key Terms Lexicon (/src/App.tsx)
Details industry standards (such as RFC 7208 (SPF), RFC 6376 (DKIM), RFC 7489 (DMARC), DNSBL, and Homoglyph Attacks) in a beginner-friendly dictionary format.pri
